  "evidencia": "Page: Verna Bloom. Sentence: She has had roles in more than 30 films and television episodes since the 1960s, including playing Mary, mother of Jesus, in \"The Last Temptation of Christ\" in 1988 and Marion Wormer in \"Animal House\" in 1978.\nPage: Animal House. Sentence: National Lampoon's Animal House is a 1978 American comedy film from Universal Pictures.\nPage: Animal House. Sentence: It was produced by Ivan Reitman and Matty Simmons, directed by John Landis, and stars John Belushi, Tim Matheson, John Vernon, Verna Bloom, Thomas Hulce, Stephen Furst, and Donald Sutherland.\nPage: Jay Cocks. Sentence: He is married to actress Verna Bloom.\nPage: Tom Hulce. Sentence: As an actor, he is best known for his role as Larry \"Pinto\" Kroger in \"Animal House\" (1978), his Academy Award-nominated portrayal of Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart in \"Amadeus\" (1984), and his role as Quasimodo in Disney's \"The Hunchback of Notre Dame\" (1996).",
