        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Verna Bloom, Jay Cocks, Tom Hulce, John Belushi, Tim Matheson, John Vernon, Thomas Hulce, Stephen Furst, Donald Sutherland, Ivan Reitman, Matty Simmons, John Landis\n- Films: Animal House, The Last Temptation of Christ, Amadeus, The Hunchback of Notre Dame\n- Companies: Universal Pictures\n- Roles: Marion Wormer, Mary mother of Jesus, Larry \"Pinto\" Kroger, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart, Quasimodo\n\nFacts:\n- Since the 1960s, Verna Bloom has had roles in more than 30 films and television episodes.\n- In 1978, Universal Pictures released National Lampoon's Animal House, an American comedy film.\n- In 1978, Animal House was produced by Ivan Reitman and Matty Simmons and directed by John Landis.\n- In 1978, Verna Bloom played Marion Wormer in Animal House.\n- In 1978, Animal House starred John Belushi, Tim Matheson, John Vernon, Verna Bloom, Thomas Hulce, Stephen Furst, and Donald Sutherland.\n- In 1978, Tom Hulce was known for playing Larry \"Pinto\" Kroger in Animal House.\n- In 1984, Tom Hulce received an Academy Award nomination for portraying Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart in Amadeus.\n- In 1988, Verna Bloom played Mary, mother of Jesus, in The Last Temptation of Christ.\n- In 1996, Tom Hulce played Quasimodo in Disney's The Hunchback of Notre Dame.\n- Jay Cocks is married to actress Verna Bloom.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
